# The kernel's size budget (audit 2026-10-29 B2-13, network audit O14), checked by tools/ksize-check.sh at every build of
# kernel.bin. One line per part: the object, its most code + data bytes, its most bss bytes. The budgets are the sizes
# of 2026-10-29 with about 3% room (the parts the kernel's shrink made smaller the same day: their new sizes); a part
# that needs more raises its line here, in the commit that grows it, so the growth is seen. The last lines bound the whole: kernel.bin's bytes, and the room it must leave on the mount tests'
# floppy (the binding limit, KERNEL_MAX_MOUNT).
# DESIGN D28 steps 2-3 (2026-10-29, the console's UTF-8): term 8,652 -> 12,558 (the decoder, the 16-bit cells and the
# scrollback's high rows, wide characters, CON_UFONT, CON_READ's 4-byte cells), gfx 6,086 -> 7,770 and bss + 260 (the
# Unicode font's lookup, byte-wise drawing, the built-in boxes, Topaz's own 0x80-0x9F kept aside), tty 2,508 -> 2,876
# (Backspace by character), confont new 3,018 (the width table 1,816, the font's checks); the mount tests' RAM disk
# went from 716 to 712 KB for it (Makefile).
# 2026-10-30 (the allocator, docs/d27-c-library.md "The allocator"): NREG 8 -> 16, proc bss 15,573 -> 17,621 (8 more
# regions of 8 bytes in each of the 32 process slots).
